+/*
+ * Phase p of a table is the tap set used when the output sample sits p/8 of
+ * a pixel from the centre tap (hc2); hc2 alone is a nearest-neighbour pick.
+ * The 3-tap and the 5-tap stock tables sweep the phases in different
+ * directions (compare coef3_M8 and coef5_M8 row 1), so the blend rows below
+ * follow each stock table's own geometry: the neighbour that gets the weight
+ * at p3/p5 is the one the stock row of the same phase gives weight to.
+ */
